{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["Lest you be ensnared — like ״יִנָּקֵשׁ נֹשֶׁה״. דָּא לְדָּא נָקְשָׁן. You must not bestir yourself to move about, to wander, and to seek after them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "דא לדא נקשן is Aramaic, literally 'this one corresponds to that one, [both are from the root] נקש'; the phrase asserts the linguistic parallel between the two cited forms. The language about not moving/wandering is rendered hyper-literally as the syntax is terse and elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:52.903644759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}